    {
      "id": "cmip6-mlotst-definition",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-mlotst-definition.md",
      "sha256": "7c9f821afb300a640b26dbd03993d309a09793518640191dc82d641f6a4f5cb5",
      "reason": "The question asks for an operator MLD built with \"the density criterion that defines mlotst\", so the exact criterion (surface-referenced ΔB = 0.0003 m s-2 ≈ Δρ 0.03 kg m-3 at local pressure, computed online each time step) sets the algorithm to implement.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute with the 0.03 kg m-3 threshold and `ref_depth` = the model's shallowest level (`mlotst` is referenced to the ocean surface, not 10 m); even then the offline MLD from monthly means is expected to come out shallower than `mlotst`.",
        "State the three residual causes (reference level, σ0 difference vs OMIP's displaced-parcel comparison at local pressure p(k), MLD-of-mean vs mean-of-MLDs) and do not treat the residual as model error; drop columns where the threshold is never reached (`mlotst` fills these differently: CESM2 0 m, GFDL-ESM4/MPI-ESM1-2-LR ≈ full column) and report the area excluded."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "Both the published mlotst and the offline operator MLD from monthly thetao/so are being compared, and this fragment says the online monthly-mean diagnostic differs from a nonlinear diagnostic computed offline from monthly means, which is the core reason the two will disagree.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "f(monthly mean) ≠ mean of f: compute each month's MLD from that month's `thetao`/`so` and then average the MLDs (diagnostic first, then average); never average temperature and salinity first.",
        "One calendar-month climatology over the 30 years is the plain mean of that month's values across years; day weights (`temporal_aggregate`) matter only when averaging across different calendar months."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The expected results require bias, RMSD and correlation only on cells where both fields are defined for all 30 months, and a ranking of the models on common cells, which is exactly this mask rule.",
      "status": "summary_fallback",
      "fallback": "the notes failed the check",
      "violations": [
        "`here` is not in the selected fragments or the question"
      ],
      "rejected_notes": [
        "Put both fields on one grid and build one mask with `build_comparison_mask` using `ocean_only=False` (the reference here is not WOA23), apply `.where(mask)` before any metric, and report the mask's cell counts with the metrics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature.md",
      "sha256": "cf8b1424a04be2e18362300d2e76d09e3f958f9d6a451c733a0cf9938968e73c",
      "reason": "The operator density must be formed from thetao, which is potential temperature referenced to 0 dbar in every model, so its use at depth in the density criterion must be stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`thetao` is potential temperature referenced to the surface: compute density by the potential-temperature route (`temperature_kind()`), never as TEOS-10 Conservative Temperature (no `bigthetao` in these models), using a fixed-reference sigma for the criterion."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-so-practical-salinity",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-so-practical-salinity.md",
      "sha256": "96f2763290996040d675ca6e8f997ea29fa320b8f6e6793bf2c6fcb739345e19",
      "reason": "Density for the operator MLD needs salinity, and CMIP6 so is Practical Salinity, with Absolute Salinity required if TEOS-10 routines are used.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`so` is practical salinity whose units string \"0.001\" does not mean the numbers need rescaling (they are already ~35); convert S_P to S_A only inside gsw/TEOS-10 density routines."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "The three models mix gn (CESM2, MPI-ESM1-2-LR curvilinear) and gr (GFDL-ESM4 regridded to 1°×1°), which affects masks, interpolation to a regular frame for Figure 1, and where operations are exact.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr`: its fields are already remapped to 1° with a regridded land–sea mask, adding an extra resolution/remapping difference, and its 100 km vs MPI's 250 km resolution gap makes narrow features non-comparable in amplitude."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
