      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "Land and below-sea-floor cells carry the 1e20 missing value, and the defined-cell masks, difference maps and area percentages all depend on proper CF masking.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "xarray decodes 1e20 to NaN by default; build each field's valid mask from the field itself (masks differ between variables of the same model) and mask weights to the same cells."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "areacello is the tracer-cell horizontal area used for the area-weighted percentages and for the total ocean area, and layer thickness needed for the level-bracketing interpolation can be recovered as volcello/areacello.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use each model's own published `areacello` (tracer-cell area) as the area weights for the >20 m and coverage percentages; total ocean area differs between models by about a per cent, so state the area each integral covers rather than rescaling."
